# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the checkout platform.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf on, so a .sh file would
# otherwise be committed or checked out with CRLF. Inside a Linux container the
# carriage return becomes part of the shebang and the process dies with
# "/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter" — an error that names neither the file nor the
# real cause.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
